ci: run the readiness and backup selftests where they can be seen (#279)

Seventeen gate selftests exist; five were named in no workflow, so they ran
only from a local pre-commit hook. A hook does not travel to a clone or to
another checkout, which is the arrangement this repository already rejects in
the header of scripts/no-published-specs.sh.

These two run on tracked files alone and start no container, measured against a
tree holding exactly what CI checks out.

The other three stay out for reasons recorded on #279: verify-branch is failing
and filed separately, and test-ids and no-personal-identity both check against
deliberately untracked data, so neither can run in CI without a decision about
what CI is allowed to see.

